      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 87. RHS profile is Tulipa x gesneriana (15), the common garden tulip; RHS says the species is of uncertain origin and most bulbs sold are hybrids, and the growing guide covers border and specialist tulips in general. NC State has no tulip page (404) and MBG found none, so only RHS is a care source: single-source, lower confidence. Toxicity: ASPCA genus page (Tulipa spp.): toxic to dogs, cats and horses, tulipalin A and B, worst in the bulb; RHS: harmful if eaten, skin allergen, pets too. Severity 1 is the agent's grading (signs listed are mild); symptom words are mapped from the ASPCA list (depression as lethargy). Watering: no page gives a dry-down rule for pots outdoors; RHS says keep well watered while in growth, let compost dry a little after planting in the cold, and not to overwater, so let_top_dry is a mapping and 7 days a guess. Summer dormancy from RHS (warm dry summer rest, lifting and drying bulbs optional). Size is RHS's upper figure (10 to 50 cm). Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
